(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-cutting-decision :authorize-forming-operation :proceed-with-metal-cutting-work :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007131-cloud-itonami-isco-7131-painters-and-related-workers-coverage" "2799007127-cloud-itonami-isco-7127-ac-refrigeration-mechanics-coverage" "2799007125-cloud-itonami-isco-7125-glaziers-coverage" "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the metal-cutting operation" "proceed with the metal-cutting work" "proceed with the forming operation" "proceed with the press brake operation" "finalize the cutting decision" "finalize the forming decision" "authorize the forming operation" "authorize the press brake operation" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment" "override safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007213), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/sheet-metal-workshop-scheduling-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :worker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7213"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007213: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7213 Sheet Metal Workers workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7213\n-- Sheet Metal Workers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the\nrollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7213\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7213\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Sheet Metal Workers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7213` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7213` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nSheet Metal Workers cut, bend and shape sheet metal on an active shop\nfloor -- real physical-safety stakes (cut hazards, machine-press\nhazards, sharp-edge handling). The controlling constraint for this\nvertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op\nthat directly finalizes a metal-cutting/forming-execution decision\n(e.g. deciding to proceed with a specific cutting or press-brake\nforming operation), or overrides a shop safety officer's judgment --\nthose decisions must always be a hard permanent block or an\nalways-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is\ndeliberately scoped to WORKSHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION\nONLY -- it never performs sheet-metal work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same Wave3 rollout) --\ncloned and read in full in this session. The physical-safety-domain\nshape (closed allowlist + always-escalate safety flag + content-based\nscope-exclusion with a self-trip regression test) was mirrored closely\nfrom that same reference, which itself carries forward the pattern\nfrom `cloud-itonami-isco-9311` (Mining and Quarrying Labourers).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7213` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for sheet metal workers,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Sheet Metal Worker\nAdvisor ⊣ SheetMetalWorkerGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct metalworking-execution authority** --\nit must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising a metal-cutting/forming-execution decision (e.g. a specific\ncutting or press-brake forming operation), or any override of a shop\nsafety officer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a cut-hazard/machine-press-hazard/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- sheet-metal-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nmetal-cutting/forming-execution decision or a shop-safety-officer-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-cutting-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`sheetmetal.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-cutting-decision`, `:authorize-forming-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-metal-cutting-work`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`sheetmetal.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-cutting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-forming-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-metal-cutting-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with metal\n   cutting or forming work, or overriding a shop safety officer's\n   judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks metal-cutting/forming-execution/safety-\n   override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a cut-hazard/machine-\n  press-hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves\n  the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the\n  hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop\n  safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  sheet-metal-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  metal-cutting/forming-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"cutting\", \"forming\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside\nthe mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a workshop coordination actor\nworking adjacent to cutting/forming work necessarily discusses those\nconcepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased\ncarelessly. `sheetmetal.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\nmetal-cutting operation\", \"authorize the press brake operation\",\n\"override the shop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching the\ntask's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`sheetmetal.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for cutting\ntask ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\") WITHOUT\ncontaining any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`sheetmetal.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7213\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7213` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7213`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-cutting-decision` or\n  `:approve-forming-operation` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a metal-cutting/forming-execution decision\n  exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For\n  a decision this severe (cut hazards, machine-press hazards), the\n  capability itself must not exist. The only op related to\n  shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the\n  need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers a metal-cutting/forming decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring earlier\n  reference actors' transaction-amount-ceiling HARD checks): rejected\n  per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  sheet-metal-materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled\n  as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  metal-cutting/forming-execution/safety-officer-override class is a\n  hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"cutting\" \"forming\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  cutting/forming/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging\n  job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale\n  text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/workshop\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered worker AND\n   workshop (`:no-worker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a\n   metal-cutting/forming-execution or safety-officer decision in any\n   respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a metal-cutting/forming-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific cutting or forming step -- it is a calendar/logistics\n   action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a cut-hazard/machine-press-\n   hazard/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety officer;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- sheet-metal-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a metal-cutting/forming-execution\n   or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na metal-cutting/forming-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific cutting or press-brake forming operation) or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`sheetmetal.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`sheetmetal.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`sheetmetal.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-cutting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-forming-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-metal-cutting-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the\n`:op` field (`sheetmetal.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with metal-cutting work or override a shop\nsafety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`sheetmetal.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Sheet Metal Workshop Scheduling Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7213"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7213"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7213)), (:test/simulator :sheetmetal.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7213 — Sheet Metal Workers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7213)))